* Asynchronous buck converter: 12 V -> 6 V, 100 kHz, 1 A load.
* M1 is a PMOS high-side switch (source at VIN, gate driven 12 V = off,
* 0 V = on, so VGS is referenced to the input rail). D1 freewheels
* during off-time; Csnub is the typical RC-snubber capacitance.
.model PMOS PMOS (LEVEL=1 VTO=0.7 KP=110u LAMBDA=0.01)
.model DW D (IS=1e-12 N=1 RS=0.05)
Vin in 0 DC 12
Vg g 0 PULSE(12 0 0 2n 2n 4.98u 10u)
M1 sw g in in PMOS w=10000u l=1u
D1 0 sw DW
Csnub sw 0 1n
L1 sw out 10u
C1 out 0 100u
RL out 0 6
.tran 20n 50u
.end
